  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Pacific Women Shaping Pacific Development</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Pacific Women Shaping Pacific Development (Pacific Women) aimed to support women in 14 Pacific countries to participate fully, freely and safely in political, economic and social life. Pacific Women supported countries to meet the commitments made in the 2012 Pacific Island Forum Leaders&apos; Gender Equality Declaration. The program focused on three key priority areas where targeted efforts are required to shift persistent disadvantage: improving women&apos;s participation in leadership and decision making; improving women&apos;s economic empowerment; and reducing violence against women.</narrative>
  </description>
